      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $8^{x+2}=10.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take $\\log_{8}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8^{x+2}&=10\\\\\\log_{8}(8^{x+2})&=\\log_{8}(10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+2=\\log_{8}(10).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2&=\\log_{8}(10)\\\\x&=\\log_{8}(10)-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{8}(10)-2$.",
